From a72fb20500db75d96d03546b82e904002371d79a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:02:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Add the dialog for the scanner portal

This commit implements org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Scanner, whose one
method, SelectScanners, shows a dialog that lists the scanners the
frontend found and returns the ids of the ones the user chose. The
backend only asks for consent; the frontend talks to the scanner.

The dialog is a GTK 3 window with a list of rows, one per scanner,
each showing the name, how it is connected and what it can scan (film,
flatbed, feeder). It honours the modal, multiple, accept_label and
title options of the frontend call. With multiple unset the rows are
radio buttons, and the first available scanner is chosen already, so
that one click is enough when there is one scanner. Scanners that are
not available are shown and cannot be chosen. The heading names the
application and the application's own title is shown under it. With
no scanners it shows an empty state.

Return chooses, Escape, Cancel and closing the window answer with the
cancelled response, and Request.Close destroys the dialog without an
answer, because the frontend answers a closed request itself.

The interface XML is copied into data/ because an installed
xdg-desktop-portal does not carry the Scanner interface yet. The copy
goes away when it does. The dialog mirrors the libadwaita one in
xdg-desktop-portal-gnome.

Tested by calling SelectScanners on a private bus with made-up
scanners, one of them unavailable: choosing the second scanner with
Return returns its id, and the layout was checked in a screenshot.
Escape, Cancel, multiple selection, Request.Close and the empty list
were not tested.
